WEBVTT

00:00:03.200 --> 00:00:05.351
Choose Help, then Demo Projects.

00:00:05.351 --> 00:00:10.797
Demo projects are ready-made practice projects built from public sequencing data.

00:00:10.797 --> 00:00:15.840
Find Human Mapping and Variants, with results, and click Download and Open.

00:00:15.840 --> 00:00:17.991
You need an internet connection.

00:00:19.090 --> 00:00:21.559
A project is one folder on your Mac.

00:00:21.559 --> 00:00:24.576
The sidebar on the left shows what it holds.

00:00:24.576 --> 00:00:26.222
Imports holds the reads.

00:00:26.222 --> 00:00:31.982
A read is the sequence of bases that a sequencer reports for one short DNA fragment.

00:00:33.080 --> 00:00:35.066
Click HG002 under Imports.

00:00:35.066 --> 00:00:42.932
HG002 is a Genome in a Bottle reference sample, from a donor who agreed to share their genome publicly.

00:00:42.932 --> 00:00:50.111
The Inspector on the right shows how many reads there are and a summary of their base quality.

00:00:51.210 --> 00:00:55.387
Results go under Analyses, and these were made in advance.

00:00:55.387 --> 00:00:57.187
Open the minimap2 result.

00:00:57.187 --> 00:00:59.132
minimap2 is a read aligner.

00:00:59.132 --> 00:01:05.469
It finds where each read best fits the reference, a 500 kb slice of human chromosome 20.

00:01:05.469 --> 00:01:09.430
Zoom in to see each read drawn at its aligned position.

00:01:10.530 --> 00:01:12.706
Click Operations in the toolbar.

00:01:12.706 --> 00:01:20.457
The Operations Panel lists each long task LGE runs, like this download, with its progress and whether it finished.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:26.234
To learn more about projects, read the manual chapter The Lungfish Project.

00:01:26.234 --> 00:01:29.350
More videos are on the Videos page of the website.
